    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several favorable matchups today, with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the card at an elite 81.87 score. His matchup against Painter is the day's primary engine; the combination of a high-ceiling hitter's park and a significant boost from SP skill makes **Gunnar Henderson** the clear focal point for production across all five categories. Following closely, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.22) and **Sam Antonacci** (65.84) are strong plays, with both benefiting significantly from dynamic platoon advantages against Elder and Martinez, respectively. **Sam Antonacci** in particular is positioned perfectly in the leadoff spot to exploit a favorable SP skill environment, providing a high floor for runs scored.\n\nIn terms of personnel adjustments, the optimizer faced a difficult choice regarding the bench. **Jorge Polanco** (50.55) was the most competitive exclusion, ultimately falling short of the starting rotation due to a combination of a lower-order lineup assignment and less favorable park factors compared to **Coby Mayo** (58.31). While **Coby Mayo** faces the same SP as **Gunnar Henderson**, his raw power potential and higher park-adjusted upside gave him the edge in the UTIL spot. We are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, specifically for **Jacob Wilson**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Kyle Tucker**. While we are projecting them into their respective slots, the volatility of these unconfirmed lineups introduces risk, particularly for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**, who face the talented Ranger Suarez; if their lineup positions drop, their current mid-50s scores will be pressured by the efficiency floor.",
